questions.explanation:
Given:

If sec 4A = cosec (3A - 50&deg;), where 4A and 3A are acute angles, find the value of cosec (A + 25&ordm;).

Formula Used:

We know that sec &theta; = cosec (90&deg; - &theta;).

Calculation:

Given sec 4A = cosec (3A - 50&deg;)

 &rArr; 4A = 90&deg; - (3A - 50&deg;)

&rArr; 4A = 90&deg; - 3A + 50&deg;

&rArr; 4A + 3A = 140&deg;

&rArr; 7A = 140&deg;

&rArr; A = 20&deg;

Now, we need to find A + 25:

&rArr; A + 25 = 20&deg; + 25&deg;

&rArr; A + 25 = 45&deg;

cosec (A + 25&ordm;) = cosec 45&deg; = √2

&there4; The correct answer is **√2**.

